@startuml
title Decision ladder — a class may raise, never lower
skinparam shadowing false

[*] --> Evaluating

state Evaluating {
  [*] --> Preflight
  Preflight : identity · actor class · warrant signature · TTL
  Preflight --> Classify : ok
  Preflight --> Deny : invalid / unregistered / expired

  Classify : action class from tool + parameters
  Classify --> Constrain : classified
  Classify --> Deny : unclassified (fail-closed)

  Constrain : non-delegable forbids · budget
  Constrain --> Inspect : clean
  Constrain --> Deny : flat forbid / budget exceeded

  Inspect : deterministic patterns · signatures
  Inspect --> Judge : clean
  Inspect --> Redact : sensitive but tolerable
  Inspect --> Deny : injection / secret / known exploit

  Judge : local model · semantic intent
  Judge --> Allow : safe
  Judge --> Redact : borderline
  Judge --> Deny : exfiltration intent
}

Allow : ALLOW -> upstream
Redact : REDACT -> transform, then upstream
Deny : DENY -> nothing runs, receipt written

Allow --> [*]
Redact --> [*]
Deny --> [*]

note right of Constrain
  Raise-only: if the class floor is
  human/destructive, an upstream ALLOW
  is raised, never lowered.
  deny > revoked/expired > human > redact > allow
end note
@enduml
